ue: the method `child().output()` is called every time `output()` is invoked unless `this.output` is already computed. This could lead to repeated computation if `output()` is called multiple times without caching the result.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java-1877:1921-4174:4315,4324:4338","promptId":"#PTE9R","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1877,"endPos":1921,"startLine":57,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":57,"endLineOffset":52,"length":45}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":4174,"endPos":4315,"startLine":112,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":114,"endLineOffset":9,"length":142},{"pos":4324,"endPos":4338,"startLine":115,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":115,"endLineOffset":22,"length":15}]}]},{"comment":"The method `firstPhaseResultsToLocalRelation` calculates the total bytes used by summing up the ramBytesUsedByBlocks of each page. This calculation is done before checking if the total exceeds 1MB, which could lead to performance issues if the list of pages is large, as it requires iterating over all pages twice (once for the sum and once for building blocks). Consider calculating and checking the bytes used incrementally while building the blocks.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java--4900:5059,5065:6336,6342:7713","promptId":"#JT59X","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/InlineStats.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"p